---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service | Remote Team Partners"
  description="The terms of service for working with Remote Team Partners: engagements, fees, replacement guarantee, and responsibilities."
  path="/terms/"
  base="../"
>
  <section class="hero hero-slim">
    <div class="wrap">
      <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="../">Home</a><span class="sep">/</span>
        <span class="cur">Terms of Service</span>
      </nav>
      <div class="sec-head left">
        <span class="eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span> Legal</span>
        <h1>Terms of Service.</h1>
        <p>Last updated: October 2026. These terms govern how we work with our clients.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="sec" style="padding-bottom:88px">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="legal-card">
        <h2>1. Our services</h2>
        <p>Remote Team Partners recruits, employs, and manages dedicated remote professionals for client businesses. Team members are employed by Remote Team Partners, not by the client. We handle contracts, payroll, benefits, HR, and compliance for the professionals assigned to you.</p>

        <h2>2. Engagements</h2>
        <p>Each engagement is confirmed in a written proposal or statement of work describing the roles, the monthly investment per professional, and the start date. An engagement begins when both parties sign the proposal.</p>

        <h2>3. Fees and payment</h2>
        <p>Fees are billed monthly in advance, one predictable invoice per professional. Invoices are due within the payment terms stated on the invoice. There are no recruitment fees at any point.</p>

        <h2>4. Replacement guarantee</h2>
        <p>If a team member does not meet your expectations, we replace them at no additional recruitment cost, subject to the terms in your proposal.</p>

        <h2>5. Client responsibilities</h2>
        <p>You are responsible for day-to-day direction of your team members, providing the tools, systems access, and information they need to do their work. You agree to treat team members professionally and in line with applicable workplace laws.</p>

        <h2>6. Confidentiality</h2>
        <p>Both parties agree to keep confidential information shared during the engagement private and to use it only for the purposes of the engagement.</p>

        <h2>7. Intellectual property</h2>
        <p>Work product created by team members in the course of your engagement is assigned to your business, as set out in your proposal.</p>

        <h2>8. Term and termination</h2>
        <p>Engagements continue on a rolling monthly basis unless your proposal states otherwise. Either party may end an engagement with the notice period stated in the proposal. Fees already paid for the current billing period are not refundable.</p>

        <h2>9. Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p>To the maximum extent permitted by law, our total liability for any engagement is limited to the fees paid for the three months before the claim arose. We are not liable for indirect or consequential losses.</p>

        <h2>10. Governing law</h2>
        <p>These terms are governed by the laws of the United States and the applicable state law of the client's place of business, unless your proposal states otherwise.</p>

        <h2>11. Changes to these terms</h2>
        <p>We may update these terms from time to time. The version in force when your proposal is signed applies to your engagement.</p>

        <h2>12. Contact</h2>
        <p>Questions about these terms: <a href="mailto:hello@remoteteampartners.com">hello@remoteteampartners.com</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
